  "notes": "Modified cash basis village, FY ended Sept 30, 2025. Governmental beginning/ending are the governmental funds fund balances (p4), which include cash, CDs and restricted cash net of payables. Business-type measure is net position (modified cash); no single total receipts printed so receipts/disbursements totals computed. Capital grants and loan payments recorded as receipts/disbursements so roll-forward 655,853+212,804-242,008+9,511=636,160 holds. The governmental total column prints transfers in 218,986 and out 228,497 (net 9,511 to enterprise funds). The Budgetary Comparison Information (p7, report p17) is not in detail: its single receipts line, Receipts and transfers 860,035, combines all funds' receipts with transfers in and has no breakdown, and per user rule 2026-10-27 the combined all-funds schedule was replaced by per-fund lines from the fund statements' columns (p4, p6). The Statement of Activities (p2, report p5) labels the governmental Taxes line as Property taxes 85,054, so it is categorized as property tax; it adds no other new lines (its figures match pp4 and 6). Balance sheet (re-check attempt 2, user rule 2026-10-27): governmental lines taken from the Balance Sheet - Modified Cash Basis - Governmental Funds (p3, Total Governmental Funds column), whose totals (assets 391,488, liabilities 9,769, fund balances 381,719) equal the government-wide governmental column (p1); fund balance by classification (Restricted 66,039, Committed 142,679, Unassigned 173,001). Business-type lines and the combined totals stay from the government-wide Statement of Net Position (p1). Read pages 1-7 of 7"
